  'patch' and 'make' are pretty much the same no matter what platform
you're on.  With DJGPP, all it requires is downloading a lot of
zipfiles from Delorie and then following the instructions (using the
DJGPP makefile).  The only hard part is unzipping the zipfiles ---
DOS-based utilities often want to truncate or trash long filenames,
which Nethack doesn't expect.

  I've patched my copy of Nethack using DJGPP, and didn't run into
any *unsurmountable* difficulties. ;)  Search Google Groups for
"group:rec.games.roguelike.nethack djgpp" and you'll find plenty
of previous discussion on the topic.

